{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty","id":1500082,"title":"Modifiers to Magick's difficulty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-18T19:50:35-08:00","id":1500082,"title":"Modifiers to Magick's difficulty","content":"Do you all agree that there must be a maximum of a +3 or -3 difficulty modifier to Magick or do you let it go past that? So, for illustration, let's say a Mage is performing a ritual on an All Hallow's Eve and by the book, if the Storyteller agrees on certain dates (or even times of the day, if one goes by Sorcere's Crusade) there's a -1 Difficulty for certain types of Magick. Let's say the PC already knows he got this free -1 difficulty on his test, yet he says he wants to spend 3 quintessence to reduce it further by -3. Do you allow such a thing or are you strict with the limit of -3/+3 modifier to the difficulty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T22:33:51-08:00","id":1500083,"title":"","content":"I do keep the cap on total modifiers. If you have a -1, you can just... not spend 3 quint and waste one. Mages don't have huge quint pools. The important thing is to remember that they're cumulative. If you have a +1 diff from something else, the -1 timing and the -3 from quint, you're at -3. So there's still plenty of use to having access to lots of bonuses here.<br /> <br /> If I was going to house rule anything, I would consider the increased difficulties for vulgar magic as penalties you can offset with bonuses instead of being the base difficulty you can't modify from.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T23:04:51-08:00","id":1500084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500083#post1500083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do keep the cap on total modifiers. If you have a -1, you can just... not spend 3 quint and waste one. Mages don't have huge quint pools. The important thing is to remember that they're cumulative. If you have a +1 diff from something else, the -1 timing and the -3 from quint, you're at -3. So there's still plenty of use to having access to lots of bonuses here.<br /> <br /> If I was going to house rule anything, I would consider the increased difficulties for vulgar magic as penalties you can offset with bonuses instead of being the base difficulty you can't modify from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I use this house rule since quite sometime ago. I mean, as you mentioned, I see vulgar magic difficulty as a kind of penalty of sorts that I allow players to offset by the available means.<br /> Likewise, I allow players to spend Quintessence (or spend more time working on a ritual, use focus, etc) to reduce it from there. I don't see a problem with that particularly. But then again, some players don't think that's enough lol, and more than once a player came to me asking that as he's spending a valuable resource (Quintessence in the aforementioned example) I should consider letting the -1 stack with the -3 of Quintessence spending, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T02:13:47-08:00","id":1500089,"title":"","content":"Not enough for what? Games have limits for a reason. Constantly pestering your ST for exceptions to make things easier feels off to me. Magic is not supposed to be easy, even with throwing everything you can at it. It's supposed to carry a bit of risk that everything blows up in your face when you use it. Even at Arete 3. Even at Arete 8.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to make magic easier/more powerful, but they all come with costs and limitations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T11:26:18-08:00","id":1500111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500089#post1500089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not enough for what? Games have limits for a reason. Constantly pestering your ST for exceptions to make things easier feels off to me. Magic is not supposed to be easy, even with throwing everything you can at it. It's supposed to carry a bit of risk that everything blows up in your face when you use it. Even at Arete 3. Even at Arete 8.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to make magic easier/more powerful, but they all come with costs and limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Enough&quot; in the sense that they want more, like in the example I gave. They think the -3 from Quinteessence should be its own thing in the sense that if they get a -1 for it being Midnight, the -3 from Quintessence should still work as it's its own thing and has nothing to do with other bonus as they're &quot;sacrificing something&quot; and then there's the talk that&quot; Every ST Tom, Dick and Harry allow me to do it, and it's cool pleeease <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:44:30-08:00","id":1500120,"title":"","content":"To which I'd just say, &quot;no.&quot; There's abundant ways to get that -3 reduction, and quintessence is a limited resources to encourage them to save it for when they really need it, not so they're constantly throwing lots of it at every spell. &quot;I want the game to be easier and my former STs let me do it,&quot; are not convincing arguments to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T13:34:14-08:00","id":1500132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500120#post1500120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To which I'd just say, &quot;no.&quot; There's abundant ways to get that -3 reduction, and quintessence is a limited resources to encourage them to save it for when they really need it, not so they're constantly throwing lots of it at every spell. &quot;I want the game to be easier and my former STs let me do it,&quot; are not convincing arguments to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, people love to complain when things get hard. Especially since many ST wants to act like mothers and spoil the players, allowing them to do anything they want and escape unharmed. I'm known in my neighborhood for being a &quot;cruel ST&quot;, I don't hesitate about killing players when they do something stupid, and I often do it.<br /> <br /> Regarding Magick, I sometimes see a -1 as a <i>basis</i>, from which it's possible to reduce it further with Quintessence, but to be honest I've never made up my mind about which one is fairer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T14:38:04-08:00","id":1500137,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure where you can measure &quot;fairness&quot; here, but if you make quintessence more powerful, you just make people want to raise Avatar higher at creation because it's so hard to raise in play based on the desire to be able to hold/spend more quintessence at once rather than caring about what having a potent Avatar is meant to represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T15:00:37-08:00","id":1500139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500137#post1500137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where you can measure &quot;fairness&quot; here, but if you make quintessence more powerful, you just make people want to raise Avatar higher at creation because it's so hard to raise in play based on the desire to be able to hold/spend more quintessence at once rather than caring about what having a potent Avatar is meant to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand your concern and I share it, but the thing is Avatar is similar to Generation (although naturally not so limiting, so to speak), it's a kind of background many players will want to have as high as the ST allow it (of course here again generation is more &quot;imbalanced&quot;, so to speak). As it happened with Generation, where I had to give up after many years of a futile battle, trying to convince my players that they don't need to take advantage of the lowest generation the ST allow them to have. I don't try anymore, it's clearly understandable they want to have Daemon as high as possible (or as many points into generation as it's possible, in the case of vampire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T07:54:01-08:00","id":1500179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500089#post1500089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are lots of ways to make magic easier/more powerful, but they all come with costs and limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>More power and increased variety for Magick Effects and other magic / occult / mystical skills and abilities can also be earned with less or very little outright costs, trade-offs, prices, or limitations; through stylish, good, polite, and interesting role-playing / gameplay participation (which can very well also include persons / friends outside the particular Chronicle's group, the whole group, and of course as well the Storyteller) .<br /> <br /> This includes choices and decisions during preparation for <i>World of Darkness </i>sessions (or sittings / meetings in regard to other role-playing / imagination games like <i>Dungeons and Dragons </i>or <i>Pathfinder</i>), in the long-term throughout the whole Chronicle and possibly beyond, and also as well complex and good decisions made on an ongoing basis during particular interesting, intricate, fun, and nice role-playing meetings / sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T15:57:43-08:00","id":1500214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500179#post1500179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More power and increased variety for Magick Effects and other magic / occult / mystical skills and abilities can also be earned with less or very little outright costs, trade-offs, prices, or limitations; through stylish, good, polite, and interesting role-playing / gameplay participation (which can very well also include persons / friends outside the particular Chronicle's group, the whole group, and of course as well the Storyteller) .<br /> <br /> This includes choices and decisions during preparation for <i>World of Darkness </i>sessions (or sittings / meetings in regard to other role-playing / imagination games like <i>Dungeons and Dragons </i>or <i>Pathfinder</i>), in the long-term throughout the whole Chronicle and possibly beyond, and also as well complex and good decisions made on an ongoing basis during particular interesting, intricate, fun, and nice role-playing meetings / sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T04:18:09-08:00","id":1500282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500214#post1500214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's an interesting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to note that creating and learning Rotes and using Conjunctional Magick Castings / Effects are discussed very often in M:tA books; as options which are outright very interesting and highly effective in regard to a Mage / Magi improving her or his variety of methods, her situational chances, and also as well overall capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-21-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T11:39:31-08:00","id":1500625,"title":"","content":"The forums are back! Yes! <br /> <br /> My own view on this matter is this: the +3 difficulty cap is problematic; if everything is going against you the problems shouldn't cap out at +3. Problems should just keep on accumulating until the Effect is nearly impossible to pull off. For example, a rank 1 Coincidental Effect is Difficulty 4; no matter how many difficult increases you suffer, RAW says that that will never be worse than Difficulty 7. <br /> <br /> As for the \u20133 cap: those difficulty reductions generally don't just happen; in practice, they usually require the mage to put some effort into arranging for them to happen. And the higher the rank of the Effect, the more work I <i>want</i> the mage to be putting into it; so I'm not going to limit how much effort he's allowed to benefit from, beyond the \u201cminimum difficulty 3\u201d cap that applies to <i>all</i> difficulties. <br /> <br /> So yeah; I ignore the \u00b13 caps on Magical Modifiers. <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T08:34:48-08:00","id":1501236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500082-modifiers-to-magick-s-difficulty?p=1500625#post1500625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forums are back! Yes!<br /> <br /> My own view on this matter is this: the +3 difficulty cap is problematic; if everything is going against you the problems shouldn't cap out at +3. Problems should just keep on accumulating until the Effect is nearly impossible to pull off. For example, a rank 1 Coincidental Effect is Difficulty 4; no matter how many difficult increases you suffer, RAW says that that will never be worse than Difficulty 7.<br /> <br /> As for the \u20133 cap: those difficulty reductions generally don't just happen; in practice, they usually require the mage to put some effort into arranging for them to happen. And the higher the rank of the Effect, the more work I <i>want</i> the mage to be putting into it; so I'm not going to limit how much effort he's allowed to benefit from, beyond the \u201cminimum difficulty 3\u201d cap that applies to <i>all</i> difficulties.<br /> <br /> So yeah; I ignore the \u00b13 caps on Magical Modifiers.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Totally agree here. If the player arranges to use &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; to find the perfect spot on the perfect Umbral Realm, collected the &quot;Dark Phoenix Flaming Fetters&quot; to use on September 9 of the year 999 which &quot;coincidentally&quot; is also the day upon which the Tiamat Dragon also completes it's 9th cosmological cicle, I want my player to unleash the &quot;Super Goo Spell&quot; at its maximum potency. Likewise, if my player is trying to do a rushed spell while being beamed by submarine Hit Markers inside of their submersed lab while the room is getting filled with water, I want them to suffer.<br /> <br /> Heck, I go even beyond the min dif of 3. For each -1 the player would get bellow dif 3, I give an extra dice. Go for it, tiger.<br /> <br /> But then again, my games usually go over the board in the spectacle side of things, so I'd say this is a matter of ST fiat and preference, but I do encourage my fellow STs to apply the Golden Rule here as they see fit - just remember to notify your players ahead of time about which houserules you'll be using, and stick with them consistently throghout the entire game.<br /> <br /> And hey, good to be back to you all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T08:47:27-08:00","id":1501238,"title":"","content":"In my silly example above, using &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; could be an adventure by it's own right (maybe you could ask them to find the &quot;Great Architect Compass&quot; just for this), reaching that perfect Umbral Realm that you found with your &quot;Krilian/Ethereal Astrolab&quot; could be another; finding and collecting the flaming feathers of a <b>Dark Phoenix</b> would certanly be an adventure, and perhaps to be able to reach the day Setember 9 of the year 999 can only be accomplished by using the special Fae Gate located in the Dream Realm of the Mushrooms.<br /> <br /> So, you could create an entire plot arc revolving around a single spell (which would probably be a &quot;world shaking&quot; spell to be worth all the fuzz), which would never happen if you can just have the same &quot;max -3&quot; just by doing it at your chantry with some herbs you can find at a market. That single spell will be far more special than a &quot;lesser version&quot;, and demand tons of research, diplomacy to find that one mountain sage who holds the lost knowledge of the &quot;legend of the Dark Phoenixes&quot;, involvement in some weird Fae war to manage to get their help in reaching the &quot;Mushroom Kingdom&quot;, and perhaps along the way some Nefandi or Techno-boys or even rival Trads that get the scent of what you're doing and now you have to race against time as they try to either get there first or burn your chances to accomplish your goal.<br /> <br /> It can cause huge changes on how your game can be/is played","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}